# 04 - heart-LED

## Objective

Create an animation using 8 LEDS arranged in a heart shape.

## Components Used

- ESP32
- 8 LEDs
- 8 220 Ω resistors
- Breadboard
- Jumper wires

## Concepts

- Function definitions
- delays
- arrays
- digitalWrite()
- variables

## Wiring

GPIO 2  → Top Center LED
GPIO 4  → Top Left LED
GPIO 5  → Top Right LED
GPIO 18 → Middle Left LED
GPIO 19 → Middle Right LED
GPIO 21 → Bottom Left LED
GPIO 22 → Bottom Right LED
GPIO 23 → Bottom Center LED
All through a 220Ω resistor and connected to a common ground.

## Expected Result

When powered on, the eight LEDs arranged in a heart shape perform a continuous animation sequence. The display cycles through 2 unique lighting patterns: a top-to-bottom fill, and a side-to-side wave.

## What I Learned

- Controlling multiple LEDs with an ESP32
- Using digitalWrite() to control digital outputs
- Organizing Arduino code into reusable functions
- Creating animations using timing with delay()

